exports[`스토리 > 1챕터 계획 1`] = `
[
  {
    "content": "You are the head writer of an anime-style gacha game (think Arknights) planning its main story chapter by chapter. You keep long-running continuity, honour the author directives exactly, and give every chapter a clear shape. Always answer with a single JSON object only — no explanations, no markdown, no code fences.",
    "role": "system",
  },
  {
    "content": "[task: story-plan chapter=1]

World: 아스트라

Setting:
하늘에 뜬 섬들 위에 세워진 마도 공학 도시. 섬을 띄우는 결정이 조금씩 빛을 잃어 가고 있다.

Premise / starting scenario:
플레이어는 변두리 섬의 수비대에 새로 부임한 지휘관이다.

AUTHOR DIRECTIVES — authoritative, they override everything else:
너무 어둡지 않게. 세 챕터마다 큰 반전이 하나 있다.

Cast (the ONLY named characters you may use; use the names exactly as written):
- 아린 (6★, 딜러, 불꽃): looks: 아린은(는) 은발에 푸른 눈을 가졌다. | personality: 아린은(는) 침착하고 말수가 적지만 동료를 아낀다.
- 세레나 (5★, 치료, 서리): looks: 세레나은(는) 은발에 푸른 눈을 가졌다. | personality: 세레나은(는) 침착하고 말수가 적지만 동료를 아낀다.
- 카이 (4★, 방어형, 전격): looks: 카이은(는) 은발에 푸른 눈을 가졌다. | personality: 카이은(는) 침착하고 말수가 적지만 동료를 아낀다.

Existing locations:
(none yet)

Story so far: nothing yet — this is the very first chapter.

Plan chapter 1.
- This is chapter 1: introduce the premise of the starting scenario and the main situation the player is thrown into.
- Re-read the author directives. If a directive is periodic or conditional (e.g. "someone dies every three chapters"), use the chapter numbers and the arc ledger above to decide whether chapter 1 must fulfil it, and if so plan it explicitly.
- Exactly 6 nodes (scenes), in reading order. Together they form one chapter with a beginning, rising tension and a closing hook.
- Use about half of the cast at most in this chapter (≤ 2 different named characters), at most 3 named characters per node. A node with no named character (narration, unnamed extras, the player alone) is fine.
- Prefer reusing existing locations; invent a new one only when the story needs it.
- synopsis: 3–5 sentences describing the whole chapter.
- node.guide: 2–4 sentences of instructions for the scene writer: what happens, the emotional turn, how it ends.
- node.location: either the exact name of an existing location (string), or a new location object {"name", "description" (one sentence), "imageTags" (English comma-separated scenery tags for an illustrator: place, architecture, time of day, weather, lighting — NO people, NO characters)}.
- Write title, synopsis, guides, location names and descriptions in Korean (한국어). Character names exactly as in the cast list. imageTags always in English.

Reply with JSON:
{"title": "...", "synopsis": "...", "nodes": [{"title": "...", "guide": "...", "cast": ["name", ...], "location": "existing name" | {"name": "...", "description": "...", "imageTags": "..."}}]}",
    "role": "user",
  },
]
`;

exports[`스토리 > 마무리 (장면 없음, 지시문 없음) 1`] = `
[
  {
    "content": "You are the story editor of an anime-style gacha game. You write precise recaps that later writers rely on for continuity. Always answer with a single JSON object only — no explanations, no markdown, no code fences.",
    "role": "system",
  },
  {
    "content": "[task: story-recap chapter=1]

Chapter 1: "흔들리는 섬"
Planned synopsis: 지휘관이 부임한 날, 섬이 크게 흔들린다. 아린과 함께 결정실로 향한다.

Full script of the chapter:
(scenes not available; outline) 지휘관이 부임한 날, 섬이 크게 흔들린다. 아린과 함께 결정실로 향한다.

Write:
- summary: 5–8 sentences. What actually happened (as written, not as planned), who changed and how (relationships, injuries, deaths, revelations, decisions), and open threads. Use character names.
- ledger: ONE line stating what this chapter did to the overall arc (e.g. "X died; the alliance broke; the gate was found"). It will be used to keep periodic author directives on schedule, so mention any event a directive cares about.
- events: the 1–3 major events of this chapter, each with "name" (a short title) and "summary" (one or two short sentences).
- people: named characters who appeared in this chapter but are NOT in the cast list (allies, rivals, officials, family, villains …), each with "name" and "summary" (one line: who they are and their part so far). Repeat an already recorded person only if something new was learned, using the exact same name. [] if none.
- items: notable objects obtained, lost, used or sought in this chapter (artifacts, keys, documents, weapons …), each with "name" and "summary" (one line: what it is and where it stands now). Same-name rule as people. [] if none.
- Write all text in Korean (한국어).

Reply with JSON:
{"summary": "...", "ledger": "...", "events": [{"name": "...", "summary": "..."}], "people": [{"name": "...", "summary": "..."}], "items": [{"name": "...", "summary": "..."}]}",
    "role": "user",
  },
]
`;

